# General Exclusion Patterns for Package Tools
#
# For RPM .spec files:
#   %exclude %{_datadir}/openssl/demos/certs/apps/*.pem
#   %exclude %{_datadir}/openssl/demos/sslecho/key.pem
#   %exclude %{_datadir}/openssl/test/recipes/*/*.priv.pem
#
# For Debian .install files:
#   # Exclude demo/test private keys - see .packaging-exclude
#   usr/share/openssl/demos/certs/apps/*.pem
#   usr/share/openssl/test/recipes/*/*.priv.pem
#
# For general build systems, exclude these directories from production:
#   demos/certs/apps/
#   test/recipes/
#
# Or include only in separate development/testing packages.

# Recommended Package Structure:
#
# openssl (production runtime)
#   - libraries (libssl, libcrypto)
#   - openssl command line tool
#   - NO demo or test private keys
#
# openssl-devel (development package)
#   - headers
#   - pkg-config files
#   - static libraries (optional)
#   - NO demo or test private keys
#
# openssl-demos (optional demo package) 
#   - demo source code
#   - demo certificates/keys with SECURITY warnings
#   - clearly marked as DEMO ONLY
#
# openssl-test (optional test package)
#   - test fixtures
#   - test private keys with SECURITY warnings
#   - clearly marked as TEST ONLY
#
# This separation ensures production packages never contain hard-coded credentials.
